{"availability":"available","full":"supnate/rekit-portal","name":"rekit-portal","description":"Web UI for managing a Rekit project.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":91,"forks":6,"created":"2016-12-22T14:32:26Z","updated":"2019-04-01T02:35:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["react","react-router","redux","rekit"],"demo":"https://rekit-portal.herokuapp.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:06.291Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:06.291Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:06.291Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:06.291Z","stars":91,"forks":6}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Rekit portal is a new dev tool shipped with Rekit 2.0. It's a central place to manage and analyze your Rekit project. Rekit portal itself is also created with Rekit, so it's also a good real-world example of Rekit for reference.","To have a quick view on how Rekit portal works, you can look at the live demo.","The most notible part of the dashboard is the overview diagram. It's an intuitive view about the architecture of a Rekit project. It's also interactive, you can mouse move to different features, components, actions to see the relationship of some specific element. You can also click a node to deep dive into it. Below information is covered by the overview diagram:"],"features":["Provide a more intuitive way to create, rename, move or delete features, components or actions than CLI. Just like you always create a Java class using an IDE like eclipse.","Generate diagram reports of the project architecture by source code. So that new team members, or yourself several months later could learn the project easier.","Easy to run tests of a single component or action by just right click on it.","Integrated test coverage report.","Relationship between modules."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/supnate/rekit-portal/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5d20b51c33